### LGPLv3 compliance

  - Desktop builds (Windows, Linux, macOS): Qt is linked dynamically as shared
    libraries (Qt6Core.dll/.so/.dylib, Qt6Quick.dll/.so/.dylib, etc.). Users
    can substitute their own modified Qt build by replacing those shared
    libraries next to the executable, satisfying LGPLv3 sec. 4(d)(0).

  - Android builds: Qt for Android is typically linked statically (this is the
    default Qt for Android packaging model — the .apk bundles the Qt runtime).
    Under LGPLv3 sec. 4(d)(1), users have the right to re-link the application
    against a modified Qt. To honour this obligation when distributing
    Android .apk / .aab artifacts, OpenTodo's release builds preserve the
    object files (.o) so a user can request the re-linkable build artifacts;
    contact the project maintainer.

  - Web (WASM) builds: Qt for WebAssembly is linked statically into the
    .wasm output. The same re-link obligation applies. The Qt source needed
    to rebuild the WASM runtime is available at the URL above
    (https://www.qt.io/download-open-source) and matches the version pinned
    by this project's build configuration (Qt 6.11.0).

  - To rebuild OpenTodo against a modified Qt, see [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md)
    and [docs/WASM.md](docs/WASM.md) for the build commands; Qt sources are
    available at the URL above.


